<BaseLayout title="Our psychology-informed approach" description="Discover Notice, Understand, Explore and Practise: a curious, neurodiversity-affirming approach.">
  <h1>Curiosity before correction</h1>
  <p>The Curious Brain Toolkit does not assume that the child is the problem or that every child needs the same strategy.</p>
  <section>
    <h2>Notice → Understand → Explore → Practise</h2>
    <Framework />
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Understanding before strategies</h2>
    <p>Consider the task, environment, predictability, relationships and support around the child, alongside their own experience.</p>
  </section>
  <a href="/resources/">Explore resources that use this approach</a>
</BaseLayout>
